on":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":52297,"output_tokens":3296,"requests":4}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a test asserting a validated live-daemon change invokes `systemctl reload docker` (SIGHUP) and never `restart`, and that a reload failure only WARNs.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC: 'A validated daemon.json change on a live daemon reloads Docker, never restarts.'","test_docker_storage_cap.py is listed as covering 'budget/split derivation, per-engine-version builder.gc rendering, idempotent merge preserving pre-existing keys, backup-restore on a rejected config' — reload-vs-restart is not among them."],"finding":"The AC 'A validated daemon.json change on a live daemon reloads Docker, never restarts' has no described proving step in the Testing section — the test files cover merge/backup-restore, per-engine rendering, observability emission, and autodeploy pruning, but none asserts that a validated change invokes `systemctl reload docker` and never `restart`.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f114f6eef814688dc","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria line 'A validated daemon.json change on a live daemon reloads Docker, never restarts' / Testing section","norm_id":"n9e71f53ea9d51086","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A regression makes the script call `systemctl restart docker` on a validated change, taking Gerrit/review-bot/MCP down — no test would catch it."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Extend test_docker_storage_cap.py with a stubbed-systemctl case: assert the reload path is taken on a validated change, restart is never invoked, and a failed reload produces a WARN naming the runbook step without restarting.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm the exact `builder.gc` policy key names and the engine version at which `maxUsedSpace`/`reservedSpace`/`minFreeSpace` replaced `defaultKeepStorage` against the engine's daemon.json reference (record MATCH + version), rather than relying on the recalled '25.0' boundary.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"Engine 25.0 / BuildKit 0.13 added `policy[].reservedSpace|maxUsedSpace|minFreeSpace` and deprecated `defaultKeepStorage`/`keepStorage`\"","Plan concedes: \"A wrong key is silently IGNORED — the cap would simply not exist\"","This is a NEW daemon.json surface for the repo (no `builder.gc`/`reservedSpace` usage found)"],"finding":"The `builder.gc` schema-key claims (maxUsedSpace at >=25.0, defaultKeepStorage below; reservedSpace/minFreeSpace) are asserted from a recalled version boundary ('Engine 25.0 / BuildKit 0.13') rather than verified against the engine's documented daemon.json reference. A wrong key is, by the plan's own account, silently ignored (the cap simply would not exist). The plan does probe and test both renderings, but the version threshold itself and the exact key names are the load-bearing facts and are UNVERIFIED.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fda33bddfd9dd6777","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design — 'The daemon.json schema is version-dependent, so it is PROBED'","norm_id":"n3d458ad4e858ee6d","priority":0.85,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The real version boundary or key name differs from the recalled 25.0 value, so the rendered `maxUsedSpace` is ignored on a 24.x engine (or vice versa) and the BuildKit cap silently does not exist"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.85,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Verify (against `dockerd --help`/docs on the pinned target engine) that `dockerd --validate --config-file` exists and rejects a schema-invalid daemon.json, and state the minimum engine version; specify what the JSON-parse-only fallback catches vs. misses so the 'changes nothing' guarantee is not overstated.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.35,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"the merged file VALIDATED (`dockerd --validate --config-file`, else a JSON parse)\"","search_files: all `--validate` occurrences in the repo are opengrep/semgrep engine calls, not dockerd — this is a NEW external capability for this codebase","The whole fail-safe promise ('a failed validation restores the backup and changes nothing') rests on this flag actually rejecting a bad config"],"finding":"The daemon-safety gate depends on `dockerd --validate --config-file` existing and behaving as a schema check on the target engine, but the plan neither pins the engine version for this flag nor cites its --help/docs; the repo has never invoked `dockerd --validate` (all existing `--validate` uses are opengrep/semgrep). The plan's own hedge ('else a JSON parse') signals uncertainty. `dockerd --validate` was added in a specific engine release and a bare JSON parse is a strictly weaker check that would not catch a schema-valid-but-semantically-rejected daemon.json.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2dd4eef2f54d83c8","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design — 'Install point, and how a LIVE daemon picks it up' (dockerd --validate --config-file)","norm_id":"n6efda67272bddbb2","priority":0.55,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Target engine lacks `dockerd --validate` and the script silently falls back to a JSON parse that passes a schema-invalid daemon.json, so a malformed cap ships and dockerd fails to start on next boot — the exact self-inflicted outage the design claims to prevent"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.55,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committe